 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration discovers scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/en/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # secret_key is the Scaleway API secret key to send in every HTTP API request during service discovery (mandatory).
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/console/account/how-to/generate-api-key/
+  - secret_key: "..."
+
+    # project is the id of the Scaleway project to discover Instances in (mandatory).
+    project: "..."
+
+    # zone is an optional zone to query Instances from.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/console/account/reference-content/products-availability/
+    # By default, fr-par-1 is used.
+    #
+    # zone: "..."
+
+    # api_url is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # api_url: "..."
+
+    # name_filter is an optional filter for returning only Instances whose name contains the given string.
+    #
+    # name_filter: "..."
+
+    # tags_filter is an optional filter for returning only Instances, which contain all the given tags.
+    #
+    # tags_filter: ["...", "..."]
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from.
+    # By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<ip>:<port>`, where `<ip>` is the public IPv4 address of the Instance, falling back to its private IP address when no public IPv4 address is assigned,
+and `<port>` is the port from the `scaleway_sd_configs` (default port is `80`). Instances without any IP address are skipped.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the id of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the id of the project the Instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone the Instance is located in.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the Instance, such as `DEV1-S`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_state`: the state of the Instance, such as `running`, `stopped`, `starting`, `stopping`, or `locked`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the Instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv6`: the public IPv6 address of the Instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ip`: the private IP address of the Instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma-separated list of tags applied to the Instance.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag, default: 30s.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
